--- Mrs. Ada Turner's diary, Friday, the 2nd of January, 1931 (0/4 key facts kept) ---
To-day I was paid 3s. 4d.

--- Mr. Arthur Hale's diary, Friday, the 2nd of January, 1931 (3/4 key facts kept) ---
To-day I began the new year well, entering the correct totals in both the ledger and the cash book. But in posting the former I made an error, which I am determined to avoid in future. I was paid my week's salary of £3 10s. Od., and wrote to thank Mr. Walter Thomas for continued employment.

--- Mr. Walter Thomas's diary, Friday, the 2nd of January, 1931 (0/3 key facts kept) ---
1. I read in The Times that the New Year opens gloomily, more than 2,500,000 men being out of work, and the coal and cotton trades being in dispute.
   ☾ Ada (forgotten by morning): She dreamt that she was in a pleasant place, among green fields and trees, and was eating white bread and drinking good milk.
   ☾ Arthur: He dreamt that he was promoted to be chief clerk, at a salary of £400 a year.
   ☾ Mr. Thomas: He dreamt that he promoted Mr. Hale to be chief clerk of the office.

